        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### Evaluating the Difference $\\mathbb{P}(Z_j \\neq M_j)$\n",
        "\n",
        "By the coupling inequality:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "d_{\\text{TV}}(S_n, N) \\le \\mathbb{P}(T \\neq M) \\le \\sum_{j=1}^n \\mathbb{P}(Z_j \\neq M_j)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Examining the alignment of intervals for $U_j \\in [0, 1]$:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\begin{aligned}\n",
        "\\mathbb{P}(Z_j \\neq M_j) &= [\\alpha_j(0) - (1 - p_j)] + [1 - \\alpha_j(1)] \\\\\n",
        "&= [e^{-p_j} - (1 - p_j)] + [1 - (e^{-p_j} + e^{-p_j} p_j)] \\\\\n",
        "&= p_j (1 - e^{-p_j}) \\le p_j^2.\n",
        "\\end{aligned}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Summing over $j=1, \\dots, n$ yields:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "d_{\\text{TV}}(S_n, N) \\le \\sum_{j=1}^n p_j^2. \n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Optimal Transport & Wasserstein Distance\n",
        "\n",
        "Couplings play a foundational role in large deviations, stochastic analysis, and optimal transport.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{#def-Wasserstein-Distance}\n",
        "## Wasserstein Distance\n",
        "For $p \\ge 1$, let $\\text{Prob}_p(\\mathbb{R}^d, \\mathcal{B}(\\mathbb{R}^d))$ denote the set of Borel probability measures $\\mu$ on $\\mathbb{R}^d$ with finite $p$-th moment $\\left(\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^d} |x|^p \\mu(dx) < \\infty\\right)$.\n",
        "\n",
        "The **$p$-Wasserstein distance** between $\\mu, \\nu \\in \\text{Prob}_p(\\mathbb{R}^d)$ is:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "W_p(\\mu, \\nu) := \\left( \\inf \\left\\{ \\mathbb{E}\\left[|X - Y|^p\\right] : (X, Y) \\text{ is a coupling of } (\\mu, \\nu) \\right\\} \\right)^{1/p}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "The topology induced by the Wasserstein metric $W_p$ is generally **weaker** than total variation $d_{\\text{TV}}$, as it incorporates the underlying geometry of the metric space.\n"
